      },
      "message": "fix(web): build-app-wasm.sh runs on stock macOS bash 3.2 and BSD sed\n\n`sed -i` is GNU-only (BSD sed takes the next argument as the backup\nsuffix), so the three in-place edits now write a temp file and move it\nback. The empty PROFILE_ARGS expansion uses the `${arr[@]+...}` form,\nwhich bash 3.2 accepts under `set -u`. sha256sum is missing on stock\nmacOS, so the checksum falls back to `shasum -a 256` when sha256sum is\nabsent. Linux and Git Bash take the same path as before.\n\nNot run on macOS or bash 3.2; the wasm build was not executed.\n\nFixes #1315\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
